    {
      "branch": "S3 posture decoder (`posture_decoder/`)",
      "class": "NUMERICALLY_VALID_BUT_SEMANTICALLY_DOWNGRADED",
      "why": "the numbers describe the DB9 released `angles` array, and that array is unchanged. But the historical canonical16 representation includes the four DIP channels, and this audit shows DIP3 and DIP5 are sign-inverted relative to the published sign criteria. Any claim of the form 'the decoder recovers physiological finger pose' is therefore unsupported for the DIP components; the classification numbers themselves stand.",
      "action": "re-describe as a decoder over the released DB9 representation, not over physiological DIP angles; no rerun required for the numbers"
    },
    {
      "branch": "S5 bridge (`bridge_audit/`)",
      "class": "NEEDS_REINTERPRETATION",
      "why": "the bridge compares DB9 against emg2pose. emg2pose supplies genuine DIP flexion; DB9's DIP3/DIP5 are inverted and its CMC5 column is the wrist channel. Any bridge conclusion that leans on those channels must be re-read.",
      "action": "re-read the per-channel contributions; the aggregate may survive"
    },
    {
      "branch": "DB9 distributional open-set (`db9_distributional_open_set/`)",
      "class": "UNCHANGED",
      "why": "the open-set work is about the distribution of the released representation. This audit does not change the release, the frames or the labels it used.",
      "action": "none"
    },
    {
      "branch": "DB9 channel validity (`db9_channel_validity/`)",
      "class": "PARTIALLY_OVERTURNED",
      "why": "its segmentation used `repetition`, which is the PRE-relabelling vector and is misaligned with `glove`/`angles` in 24 of 99 files; and it grouped by a container count in places. Its per-channel statistics are therefore computed on shifted boundaries. This audit re-derives the same questions on `restimulus x rerepetition` and reaches a partly different answer: six of its suspects are exonerated at >= 0.90 subject-level agreement, while DIP3/DIP5/CMC5 are confirmed bad and DIP4/PIP3/PIP4/DIP2 are held INCONCLUSIVE.",
      "action": "keep the artifacts; do not cite the numbers; supersede with this lane"
    },
    {
      "branch": "coordinate audit (`pose_coordinate_audit/`)",
      "class": "UNCHANGED by this lane; its own outstanding items remain open",
      "why": "the earlier finding that part of that lane compared the adapter against itself, and that its PCA scripts grouped by `repetition`, is independent of this audit and is neither fixed nor re-opened here. This audit independently confirms the `repetition`-vs-`rerepetition` defect class: `repetition` is misaligned in 24 of 99 files.",
      "action": "PI decision still outstanding on the correction branch"
    },
    {
      "branch": "the in-file `subject` field as an identity key (anywhere)",
      "class": "INVALID",
      "why": "the in-file `subject` field is source-database-local. `S68_E2_A1.mat` reports `subject == 1`, colliding with `S1_E2_A1.mat`; 10 such collisions exist among the 37 Exercise B files. Any grouping by that field merges distinct people.",
      "action": "use the archive slot / filename as the identity; the historical lane `data/ninapro_db9/dataset.meta.json` already records this correctly, so this is a warning, not a live defect"
    }
  ],
